From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:37:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] wan: automatic uplink (eth0, else the WiFi client) as
 the default

wan.conf gains interface=auto, now shipped and the fallback for a missing
or unknown value. eth0 and wlan0 are then both WAN ifaces (@wan_ifaces in
the filter and nat tables, route_localnet, dnsmasq no-dhcp-interface), and
the kernel's route metric picks the one in use: eth0's udhcpc route
(metric 0) while it has a cable and a lease, the WiFi client's dhcpcd route
(3000+) otherwise. A fresh box with neither is offline and needs no change
once a cable or a WiFi network appears. The box never rewrites wan.conf, and
a pinned eth0 or wlan0 keeps its previous behaviour.

Auto only:
- S30eth sets ignore_routes_with_linkdown on eth0, so an unplugged eth0's
  lease route is skipped; `linkdown`/`linkup` drop and restore eth0's DNS
  servers, and a static (exclusive) list is registered only with carrier.
- S46wanwatch acts on eth0 carrier edges and tracks the default route in
  use; when it moves (or eth0 was re-addressed) `S60routing uplink` runs
  `rnsbox-portal ctflush`, a netlink flush of the conntrack entries that
  nftgen's masquerade rule marks, so NATed flows reconnect over the new
  uplink instead of hanging on the old address. LAN, HaLow (sl0) and
  inbound entries are kept.

Also: nftgen drops WAN packets to 127.0.0.0/8 before the open ports; the
portal shows "auto -> <iface>" and the pinned iface's own gateway; the WiFi
tab notes when the WAN is pinned to eth0; step-1 NTP and S45ntpsync count
only default routes with carrier; regen_dnsmasq no longer prints busybox
sed's cut-off lines.
